{
  "about": "The app-path grammar's cases, read by both `src/volume/path_grammar_test.rs` and `apps/desktop/src/lib/path/grammar.test.ts`, so Rust and TypeScript can't disagree. `flavor` is the local backend's: `posix` (macOS, Linux) or `windows`. `kind` null means the text is no app path at all. A scheme URL's root, root-ness, and segments belong to its volume, not the grammar, so they read null; its parent and basename are plain slash arithmetic. `parent` is null at a root: there is no parent inside the volume. `shown` is what a person reads; `fromUserInput` is what typed or pasted text becomes before it goes on the wire.",
